{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7HLT3tMgeUunM4nkJWy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I drafted the summary below. Two gaps in the plan need answers before you submit, and reviewers will likely spot both:\n\n1. **The $33,000-a-year shortfall.** The attorney costs $78,000 a year and the foundation pays at most $45,000. The summary has to say where the other $33,000 comes from each year. If the answer is the county contract, say so. But that contract is up for renewal in October, so reviewers may ask what happens if it isn't renewed.\n2. **The attorney leaving in June.** If the grant-funded hire just fills that seat, you'll still have two attorneys, and the \"third attorney\" framing falls apart. The summary needs a sentence on how the departing attorney's position will be filled.\n\nI left brackets for both. Once you tell me the answers, I'll fill them in.\n\n<final_document>\n**Project Summary**\n\n[Clinic Name] requests $90,000 over two years ($45,000 per year) to hire a third staff attorney to represent low-income tenants facing eviction in [County].\n\n**The need.** Last year, 1,140 eviction cases were filed in [County]. Our two attorneys represented the tenant in 163 of them, about 14 percent. We turned away roughly 300 more tenants who asked for help because no attorney was free. Each of our attorneys carries about 80 open cases, which is as many as we can handle responsibly.\n\n**Our results.** In the cases where we represented the tenant last year, 58 percent ended with the tenant staying in the home or getting at least 60 days to move. That is enough time to find new housing.\n\n**The project.** At our current pace of about 80 cases per attorney per year, a third attorney would let us represent about 80 more tenants each year, or about 160 over the grant period. That would cut the number of tenants we turn away by roughly a quarter. [One of our current attorneys leaves in June; that position will be filled by/with ________, so the grant-funded attorney is a net addition to our staff.]\n\n**Budget.** The position costs $78,000 a year including benefits. The Foundation's grant would cover $45,000 a year, and the remaining $33,000 a year will come from [source]. [Clinic Name] also receives $60,000 a year from [County] under a contract that comes up for renewal in October [status/expectation].\n\n**Measuring success.** We will track cases opened, tenants turned away, and case outcomes (tenant stays in the home or gets at least 60 days to move), and report these to the Foundation [every six months].\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes on choices I made:\n\n- **About 260 words now.** That leaves room for the bracketed sentences, but keep each one short.\n- **The 80-cases-a-year figure is my estimate.** I got it by splitting your 163 cases between two attorneys. If your actual closings per attorney are different, use your real number and adjust the 160 and the \"roughly a quarter.\"\n- **The 58% stands on its own.** I didn't compare it to tenants without a lawyer or call it an improvement, since you don't have that data. If you can cite a statewide or national study of outcomes for unrepresented tenants, one sentence of that would make this section stronger."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5415,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5415},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67729faa-8a54-4cf3-8860-e2f521bf5708","uuid":"9fc0e63c-b86b-4bcd-85b0-3a9251996aee","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:02:36.448Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7HLSqVG9eBHcnx6yW1c"}
